language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ abbots_puzzle: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ If 100 bushels of corn were distributed among 100 people such that each man received three bushels, each woman two, and each child half a bushel, and there are five times as many women as men, find the number of men, women, and children.
$
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/abbots_puzzle.html
$ Save this model as model.eprime and run it with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the solution is
$ written to `model.eprime.solution`:
$   savilerow model.eprime -run-solver

$ men: the number of men
find men : int(0..100)
$ women: the number of women
find women : int(0..100)
$ children: the number of children
find children : int(0..100)

branching on [men, women, children]

such that
$ the 100 people are men, women and children
men + women + children = 100,
$ there are five times as many women as men
women = 5 * men,
$ the 100 bushels: each man gets 3, each woman 2 and each child half a bushel (the whole equation is doubled to stay in integers)
6 * men + 4 * women + children = 200
